        "original_target": "If d1 d0 = 0 then kappa1 is well defined on Q1 and 0 -> H1 -> Q1 -> im(d1) -> 0 is exact with no canonical splitting; every class has exactly one diagnostic class; Phi1 = 0 exactly for ExactClass; Phi1, Gamma2 >= 0 and Gamma2 <= ||d1|| Phi1 under the norm hypothesis.",
        "source_scope_review": "The source Obstruction.lean proves kappa_well_defined and kappa_exact_sequence in general (on Add types) but never states \"no canonical splitting\", and its ratio bound takes the operator bound as a hypothesis. Mined: Q1, Repair, kappa, H1, kappa_exact_sequence, closure_charge_le_opnorm_mul_phi, closure_ratio_*; the two DerivationDagQMClosure anchors in the paper pin are fixed arithmetic. Proved here over a field: exactness and the dimension count, the conditional non-splitting (invariance under 1 + incl f pi; false when H1 = 0 or d1 = 0), uniqueness of the class, Phi1 = 0 iff zero class for definite J (false for a seminorm), and Gamma2 <= c Phi1 with the explicit column form of the operator-norm hypothesis and its necessity. External source hashes match the pins (Obstruction.lean, derivation_dag_witnesses.rs); the paper pin tfq_0345 is a CRLF-era hash.",
